// 1 -> state 2) so the FCSM emits a minimum number of CR(0x44) packets in
// state==1 before allowing exit to state==2, ensuring the asymmetric peer's
// RX framer has time to byte-align onto a CR.  See file header in
// src/rtl/local_overrides/WlinkGenericFCSM_6.v.
${TIDELINK_HOME}/src/rtl/local_overrides/WlinkGenericFCSM_6.v
// SoC Labs tdif-08 L4: route LL_RX framer through local override that adds
// a post-reset hunt_holdoff gate on the is_long_pkt → state==1 transition,
// killing the slave-side asymmetric stuck-at-state==1 bug triggered by
// training filler bytes. See src/rtl/local_overrides/WlinkRxLinkLayer.v.
${TIDELINK_HOME}/src/rtl/local_overrides/WlinkRxLinkLayer.v
